  <ym-title|Finite price recurrence and endpoint
  estimate><label|finite-price-recurrence-and-endpoint-estimate>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>Unit: YM-000026, selected-scale trace producer.

    <item>Status: draft; the finite scalar induction is proved in prose, and
    the local insertion/uniqueness mechanism is expanded. The paid cone and
    source geometric receipts are mapped exactly; selected history production
    remains upstream.

    <item>Imported Lean revision: <verbatim|3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464>.

    <item>Manuscript: <verbatim|manuscript/existence/trace-price-recurrence.tex>.
  </itemize-minus>

  <section|Source crosswalk><label|source-crosswalk>

  <block|<tformat|<twith|table-width|1par>|<twith|table-hmode|exact>|<cwith|1|-1|1|-1|cell-hyphen|t>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-bborder|1ln>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-valign|bottom>|<table|<row|<cell|<strong|Mathematical
  content>>|<cell|<strong|Exact declaration and path>>|<cell|<strong|Checked
  correspondence and remaining status>>>|<row|<cell|Scale prices and one-step
  multiplier>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Bid.gainChart>, <verbatim|YM.Bid.puffs>,
  <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Quince.cameo>,
  <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Quince.cameo_next>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Bid/Loan.lean>, <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Quince/Nectar.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Quince/Apace.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|gainChart(H,k,j)=exp((S_k-S_j)/8)>
  and <verbatim|puffs(L)=L^(1/8)>, with <verbatim|S_{j+1}-S_j=log L_j>, hence
  <verbatim|Gamma_j=Gamma_{j+1}p_j>. The monitor square root
  <verbatim|cameo(j+1)> is the fine monitor <verbatim|coinP> at the successor
  side and current coupling.>>|<row|<cell|Buffer
  inequalities>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Quince.ordered>,
  <verbatim|tillP>, <verbatim|till_gain>, <verbatim|bear>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Quince/Nectar.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|ordered>
  follows from the delayed rise condition and <verbatim|cameo_next>, giving
  <verbatim|c_{j+1}\<less\>=2c_j>. <verbatim|tillP> gives
  <verbatim|1\<less\>=P_j> and <verbatim|4P_j\<less\>=puffs(L_j)>.
  <verbatim|till_gain> gives <verbatim|2P_j b_j\<less\>=1/3>; therefore
  <verbatim|P_j b_j\<less\>=1/6>, as used in the stronger <verbatim|23/30>
  recurrence factor. The rise condition is an explicit selected-profile
  input.>>|<row|<cell|Exact local adjacent-level analytical
  inequality>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Quince.rideE>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Quince/Pride.lean>>|<cell|For every
  epsilon\<gtr\>0 it is eventually uniform in the volume, over all N and
  adjacent coefficient pairs with format/remBound, exact density transition,
  and legal adjacent sites. Its output is the local response error with
  <verbatim|sprite*(core+successor cost)> plus <verbatim|epsilon*(previous
  cost + P*weighted core + rate*successor cost)>. In manuscript these are the
  terms <verbatim|s_j> and <verbatim|epsilon_j>.>>|<row|<cell|Geometry
  preparation for the local estimate>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Quince.Cashbox>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Quince/Soot.lean>>|<cell|Supplies the
  large-volume side constraints, blend of neighboring thresholds, order
  conditions, and the exact local <verbatim|Stepper> data needed by
  <verbatim|rideE>. <verbatim|rideE> first obtains these conditions uniformly
  by taking volume large.>>|<row|<cell|Local insertion and density
  matching>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Extra.Histories.Surrey.include_one>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Quince/Surrey.lean>>|<cell|From a
  formatted next-level coefficient with remainder budget <verbatim|v>,
  constructs a formatted predecessor with pushed density; remainder budget
  <verbatim|P*size(vowel(core))+rate*v>; and coefficient error from the block
  lead at most <verbatim|sprite*(size(core)+v)>. This is the intermediate
  coefficient used in the manuscript proof of (ex-lattice-price-one-step).
  The coordinatewise construction is <verbatim|individual> followed by
  <verbatim|atom_total>; the manuscript records their finite-sum mathematical
  purpose.>>|<row|<cell|Finite-volume uniqueness from equal local
  densities>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Quince.unique_part>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Quince/Unum.lean>>|<cell|If two formatted
  coefficients on a torus of side <verbatim|n> have equal density, remBound
  budgets <verbatim|a,b>, and <verbatim|10*(h*(4*B+2)+2*B)\<less\>n>, then
  their coefficient difference is at most
  <verbatim|fineK(F)*exp(-supportExponent*h)*(a+b)>. <verbatim|fineK> is
  test-price times the sum of local probe prices times the gauge factor. The
  proof takes the signed union of regular expansions, uses total mass
  \<less\>=a+b, annihilates nonwrapping terms using the projection condition,
  and sums the exponential support tail over the finite coefficient-recovery
  probes. This is the local uniqueness argument expanded in the manuscript;
  no arbitrary density-equality-to-coefficient-equality inference is
  made.>>|<row|<cell|Tail estimate for recovery
  probes>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Quince.loom_s>,
  <verbatim|prime_fuel>, <verbatim|Local.Readable>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Quince/Lilt.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Quince/Unison.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Local/*>>|<cell|The <verbatim|loom_s> estimate bounds
  each probe by its price times the gauge factor and
  <verbatim|exp(-supportExponent*h)> times the total source mass.
  <verbatim|Local.Readable> provides finite coefficient recovery. These
  hypotheses and factors are the exact basis of the uniqueness
  proof.>>|<row|<cell|Weighted size cost of
  insertion>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Quince.spends>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Quince/Nectar.lean>>|<cell|The block cap
  and shape estimate imply <verbatim|size(v)\<less\>=P_j*size(lead(v))>. This
  is the second inequality used in the finite induction.>>|<row|<cell|Actual
  selected transition supplies the atom estimates>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Quince.Cashbox>,
  <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Quince.mosaic>,
  <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Quince.primaryT>,
  <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Quince.salaryT>,
  <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Quince.gasT>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Quince/Soot.lean>, <verbatim|Kiosk.lean>,
  <verbatim|Harvest.lean>, <verbatim|Soil.lean>,
  <verbatim|Gas.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|Cashbox> obtains the
  <verbatim|Stepper> used by <verbatim|rideE> from the selected adjacent
  transition. <verbatim|mosaic> fills its three fields with the basis-atom
  estimate <verbatim|primaryT>, the regular-atom estimate <verbatim|salaryT>,
  and the forced-slot estimate <verbatim|gasT>, under the stated
  <verbatim|Nest>, <verbatim|Arrives>, <verbatim|Medal>, <verbatim|Bunk>,
  geometry, and block hypotheses. <verbatim|Soot.parliament> supplies the
  delayed threshold for the profile <verbatim|Soot> property;
  <verbatim|Cashbox> applies it to the required transition and gets the
  <verbatim|Bunk> and <verbatim|Medal> witnesses. The manuscript expands the
  subsequent finite/countable atom aggregation and the recurrence, but does
  not rederive the internal local-card estimates of those three producers;
  their exact source path and hypotheses are recorded here rather than
  silently treating an arbitrary <verbatim|Stepper> as
  produced.>>|<row|<cell|Paid cone bound>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Work.G09.answer>,
  <verbatim|YM.Work.G09.cost_finest>, <verbatim|YM.Work.G09.cone_cost>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Work/G09.lean>; definition <verbatim|YM.Bid.G09>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Bid/Loan.lean>>|<cell|Under the <verbatim|roomCost> and
  <verbatim|Bank> inequalities, a paid comparison with <verbatim|Woke> data
  satisfies <verbatim|gainChart(H,k,j)*(cost_j+coeffSize_j)\<less\>=4*(1+columns_k)*w>
  for every rung. <verbatim|Work/G09> proves this by converting its
  <verbatim|direction> inequalities to scalar cone bounds and applying the
  bank arithmetic. The recurrence chapter matches these data to the canonical
  human-readable proof in <verbatim|sec:reference-cone> and
  <verbatim|eq:reference-gain>; it does not duplicate that cone
  argument.>>|<row|<cell|Endpoint scale iteration>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Quince.pricey>,
  <verbatim|.ascend>, <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Quince/Apace.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|pricey>
  is the one-step propagation with <verbatim|t/Gamma> cone budgets and
  normalized allowance <verbatim|t/(Gamma*cameo)>. <verbatim|ascend>
  intersects the finitely many eventual volume sets over
  <verbatim|j=m,...,k-1>, initializes from the zero left coefficient, applies
  <verbatim|Work.G09.answer> at every rung, and concludes the endpoint
  estimate. The displayed scalar proof reorganizes these steps; the exact
  factor is 23/30 (the formal proof uses a looser 1/3 allowance for the
  sprite term and still closes at 14/15).>>|<row|<cell|Public
  use>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Accent.prevails>, <verbatim|.riches>,
  <verbatim|YM.Trace.Terrace.purchasing>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Soot/Skein.lean>, <verbatim|Coffer.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Terrace/Casa.lean>>|<cell|The finite
  Coffer route calls the selected endpoint estimate at terminal scale k with
  budget <verbatim|q>; its <verbatim|b'> is the monitor square root
  <verbatim|cameo(k)> and its endpoint constant is
  <verbatim|4*(1+columns_k)>. The public Bill specialization is documented in
  <verbatim|trace-coffer-supplier.tex>.>>>>>

  <section|Checks and open dependencies><label|checks-and-open-dependencies>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>Read-only commands actually run: <verbatim|rg -n> and <verbatim|sed
    -n> on the declarations/paths in the crosswalk, including
    <verbatim|Bid/Loan.lean>, <verbatim|Work/G09.lean>,
    <verbatim|Apace.lean>, <verbatim|Pride.lean>, <verbatim|Nectar.lean>,
    <verbatim|Dawn.lean>, <verbatim|Glee.lean>, <verbatim|Soot.lean>,
    <verbatim|Surrey.lean>, <verbatim|Unum.lean>, <verbatim|Lilt.lean>,
    <verbatim|Kiosk.lean>, <verbatim|Harvest.lean>, <verbatim|Soil.lean>,
    <verbatim|Gas.lean>, <verbatim|Cache.lean>, and <verbatim|Guild.lean>.

    <item><verbatim|python3 scripts/check_blueprint.py> was attempted; it
    cannot run in this isolated clone because
    <verbatim|blueprint/units/YM-000026/unit.json> is absent. Parent
    integration has the shared unit metadata. No Lean source was edited and
    no Lean or TeX build was run.

    <item><verbatim|pricey>/<verbatim|ascend> are humanized as a finite
    recurrence, including the buffer constants and local
    insertion-versus-uniqueness decomposition. The paid-cone proof is
    cross-referenced to the canonical prose in
    <verbatim|sec:reference-cone>/<verbatim|eq:reference-gain>, whose
    assumptions are matched explicitly in the recurrence manuscript. The
    selected history must still produce its room/bank/rise conditions. The
    local support-probe tail inequality is source-proved in
    <verbatim|loom_s>/<verbatim|unique_part>; its mathematical mechanism is
    given, while its local-probe construction is a source crosswalk rather
    than a full rederivation of the underlying lattice tests.
  </itemize-minus>

